  "body": "## Summary\nThe `maxNumLimitsPerSide` constraint enforces a cap on the number of orders per side in the limit order book. However, expired or orders are not explicitly filtered or removed before enforcing this constraint. This oversight allows for griefing the system by occupying book space with expired orders, effectively preventing valid limit orders from being posted.\n\n## Finding Description\nThe `_processLimitAskOrder()` function enforces a hard cap on the number of active ask orders:\n\n```solidity\nif (ds.askTree.size() == maxNumLimitsPerSide) {\n    ...\n    revert MaxOrdersInBookPostNotCompetitive();\n}\n```\nHowever, `ds.askTree.size()` includes all orders, regardless of whether they are expired or actionable. There is no logic to remove, or invalidate expired limit orders before this capacity check.\n\nAs a result, more competitive and valid limit orders may be denied simply because the book is perceived as full, even though many of the resident orders are inactive or expired.\n\n## Impact\nMedium —  \n  1. freezing one side of the book.\n\n  2. Market Disruption — Traders may experience unfair rejection of competitive orders.\n\nPotential for Censorship — Malicious actors could selectively deny participation for specific price ranges or actors since at order posting expiration range isn't checked\n\n\n## Recommendation\nIntroduce expirationTimestamp range Field when posting new orders\n\nSkip or evict expired orders before evaluating `maxNumLimitsPerSide`.",
  "proof_of_concept": "Copy and paste the test function in the `CLOBPost.t.sol`\n\n```solidity\n function testPostLimitOrder_MaxOrdersWithExpiredOrders_Starvation_POST_ONLY() public {\n    // This test demonstrates that expired orders are counted toward maxNumLimitsPerSide,\n    // and that a valid POST_ONLY order cannot be placed even if all existing orders are expired.\n\n    address user = users[0];\n    uint256 amountInBase = 1 ether;\n    uint256 price = 100 ether;\n\n    // Set maxNumLimitsPerSide to a small value for easier testing\n    uint256 maxLimits = 3;\n    vm.prank(address(clobManager));\n    clob.setMaxLimitsPerTx(uint8(maxLimits));\n\n    // Place maxNumLimitsPerSide POST_ONLY orders, all with expired cancelTimestamps and high prices\n    for (uint256 i = 0; i < maxLimits; i++) {\n        setupTokens(Side.BUY, user, amountInBase, price + i * 10 ether, true);\n\n        ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs memory args = ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n            amountInBase: amountInBase,\n            clientOrderId: 0,\n            price: price + i * 10 ether,\n            cancelTimestamp: uint32(block.timestamp - 1), // Expired timestamp\n            side: Side.BUY,\n            limitOrderType: ICLOB.LimitOrderType.POST_ONLY\n        });\n\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        clob.postLimitOrder(user, args);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    // Now, try to place a new valid POST_ONLY order at a price that would NOT cross the book\n    setupTokens(Side.BUY, user, amountInBase, price - 10 ether, true);\n\n    ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs memory validArgs = ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n        amountInBase: amountInBase,\n        clientOrderId: 0,\n        price: price - 10 ether, // Lower than any existing order, so would not fill\n        cancelTimestamp: uint32(block.timestamp + 1 days), // Valid timestamp\n        side: Side.BUY,\n        limitOrderType: ICLOB.LimitOrderType.POST_ONLY\n    });\n\n    vm.startPrank(user);\n    // Expect revert due to starvation (expired orders still counted towards maxNumLimitsPerSide)\n    vm.expectRevert(CLOB.MaxOrdersInBookPostNotCompetitive.selector);\n    clob.postLimitOrder(user, validArgs);\n    vm.stopPrank();\n}\n```\n\nNote: `MAX_NUM_LIMITS_PER_SIDE` was set to a small value(3)",
